          "quote": "The usual plural of person is people: three people, most people. Persons is used in formal and legal language and on official signs and notices: persons under eighteen, all persons present. In everyday speech and writing, use people. In job titles, -person replaces -man when the sex of the person is unknown or does not matter: chairperson, spokesperson.",
          "severity": "minor",
